---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
---

<GuideLayout
  title="How to Brew the Perfect V60 Pour Over"
  description="A complete step-by-step guide to brewing V60 pour-over coffee. Learn timing, pouring technique, grind size, and how to troubleshoot common mistakes."
  headline="How to Brew the Perfect <em>V60 Pour Over</em>"
  subtitle="The V60 is the gold standard of pour-over coffee. Master it, and you'll unlock more flavour from your beans than any other home method."
  heroAccent="v60"
  readTime="10 min"
  category="Brew Guide"
>

<h2>What You'll Need</h2>

<div class="equipment-grid">
  <div class="equip-card">
    <div class="equip-icon">⚖️</div>
    <div class="equip-name">Scale</div>
    <div class="equip-note">0.1g accuracy preferred</div>
  </div>
  <div class="equip-card">
    <div class="equip-icon">🫖</div>
    <div class="equip-name">Gooseneck Kettle</div>
    <div class="equip-note">For precise pouring control</div>
  </div>
  <div class="equip-card">
    <div class="equip-icon">⏱️</div>
    <div class="equip-name">Timer</div>
    <div class="equip-note">Built into Brewio</div>
  </div>
  <div class="equip-card">
    <div class="equip-icon">🔧</div>
    <div class="equip-name">Burr Grinder</div>
    <div class="equip-note">Consistent grind matters</div>
  </div>
  <div class="equip-card">
    <div class="equip-icon">📐</div>
    <div class="equip-name">V60 Dripper</div>
    <div class="equip-note">Size 02 for 1–4 cups</div>
  </div>
  <div class="equip-card">
    <div class="equip-icon">📄</div>
    <div class="equip-name">V60 Filters</div>
    <div class="equip-note">Hario tabbed or untabbed</div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>The Recipe</h2>

<div class="recipe-card">
  <div class="recipe-grid">
    <div class="recipe-item">
      <span class="recipe-val">15 g</span>
      <span class="recipe-label">Coffee</span>
    </div>
    <div class="recipe-item">
      <span class="recipe-val">250 ml</span>
      <span class="recipe-label">Water</span>
    </div>
    <div class="recipe-item">
      <span class="recipe-val">93°C</span>
      <span class="recipe-label">Temperature</span>
    </div>
    <div class="recipe-item">
      <span class="recipe-val">Medium</span>
      <span class="recipe-label">Grind Size</span>
    </div>
    <div class="recipe-item">
      <span class="recipe-val">1:15</span>
      <span class="recipe-label">Ratio</span>
    </div>
    <div class="recipe-item">
      <span class="recipe-val">3:00</span>
      <span class="recipe-label">Total Time</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>Step-by-Step Brew Guide</h2>

<div class="steps">
  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-marker">
      <span class="step-num">1</span>
      <div class="step-line"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <div class="step-time">0:00</div>
      <h3>Rinse the Filter</h3>
      <p>Place the filter in the V60, set it on your mug or server, and pour hot water through the filter to rinse it. This removes the papery taste and preheats the dripper. <strong>Discard the rinse water.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-marker">
      <span class="step-num">2</span>
      <div class="step-line"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <div class="step-time">0:00</div>
      <h3>Add Coffee & Level the Bed</h3>
      <p>Add 15g of medium-ground coffee to the filter. Give it a gentle shake to flatten the bed — an even surface ensures even extraction. Place everything on the scale and tare it to zero.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-marker">
      <span class="step-num">3</span>
      <div class="step-line"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <div class="step-time">0:00 – 0:45</div>
      <h3>The Bloom</h3>
      <p>Start your timer and pour <strong>30–45ml</strong> of water in a slow spiral, just enough to saturate all the grounds. You'll see them puff up and release CO₂ — this is the bloom, and it's a sign of fresh coffee.</p>
      <div class="step-detail">
        <strong>Why it matters:</strong> Trapped CO₂ repels water. If you skip the bloom, the water channels around dry pockets instead of extracting evenly. Give it 30–45 seconds to fully degas.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-marker">
      <span class="step-num">4</span>
      <div class="step-line"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <div class="step-time">0:45 – 1:45</div>
      <h3>First Pour</h3>
      <p>Pour in a slow, steady spiral from the center outward, then back in. Avoid pouring directly on the filter paper. Add water until you reach <strong>150ml</strong> on the scale. The stream should be about the thickness of a pencil.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-marker">
      <span class="step-num">5</span>
      <div class="step-line"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <div class="step-time">1:45 – 2:30</div>
      <h3>Second Pour</h3>
      <p>Once the water level drops to about 1cm above the coffee bed, begin your second pour. Same spiral technique, bringing the total to <strong>250ml</strong>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-marker">
      <span class="step-num">6</span>
      <div class="step-line"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <div class="step-time">2:30 – 3:00</div>
      <h3>The Swirl & Drawdown</h3>
      <p>After your final pour, give the V60 a gentle swirl — just one rotation. This settles the grounds into a flat bed, which promotes even extraction during the final drawdown. The last drop should fall around the <strong>3:00 mark</strong>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>Reading Your Bed</h2>

<p>After the brew, look at the coffee bed inside the filter. It tells you a lot:</p>

<div class="bed-grid">
  <div class="bed-card bed-card--good">
    <div class="bed-visual">
      <div class="bed-line bed-line--flat"></div>
    </div>
    <h3>Flat, Even Bed ✓</h3>
    <p>Extraction was even. Your technique and grind size are dialed in.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="bed-card bed-card--high">
    <div class="bed-visual">
      <div class="bed-line bed-line--dome"></div>
    </div>
    <h3>Dome / High Sides</h3>
    <p>Grounds stuck to the sides. Pour more toward the edges, or your pour was too aggressive.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="bed-card bed-card--crater">
    <div class="bed-visual">
      <div class="bed-line bed-line--crater"></div>
    </div>
    <h3>Crater / Channel</h3>
    <p>Water channeled through one spot. Your pour was uneven or your grind is too coarse.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>Troubleshooting</h2>

<div class="trouble-table">
  <div class="tt-row">
    <div class="tt-problem">Brew finished in under 2:30</div>
    <div class="tt-cause">Grind is too coarse</div>
    <div class="tt-fix">Grind finer (one click at a time)</div>
  </div>
  <div class="tt-row">
    <div class="tt-problem">Brew took longer than 3:30</div>
    <div class="tt-cause">Grind is too fine</div>
    <div class="tt-fix">Grind coarser</div>
  </div>
  <div class="tt-row">
    <div class="tt-problem">Tastes sour and thin</div>
    <div class="tt-cause">Under-extracted</div>
    <div class="tt-fix">Grind finer or increase water temperature</div>
  </div>
  <div class="tt-row">
    <div class="tt-problem">Tastes bitter and dry</div>
    <div class="tt-cause">Over-extracted</div>
    <div class="tt-fix">Grind coarser or lower water temperature</div>
  </div>
  <div class="tt-row">
    <div class="tt-problem">Uneven, muddy taste</div>
    <div class="tt-cause">Channeling</div>
    <div class="tt-fix">Even your pour, level the bed before brewing</div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="tip-callout">
  <div class="tip-icon">💡</div>
  <div>
    <strong>Keep a brew journal.</strong> The single most effective way to improve your V60 is to log what you did and what it tasted like. After 10–15 entries, you'll see clear patterns in what works for your setup. That's exactly what Brewio is built for.
  </div>
</div>


<aside class="tool-promo">
  <a href="/tools/brew-timer/">
    <span class="tp-label">Time your V60 brew</span>
    <span class="tp-desc">Step-by-step timers with the same timings as this guide, running in the browser.</span>
  </a>
</aside>

</GuideLayout>

<style>
  /* ── Equipment Grid ── */
  .equipment-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .equip-card {
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .equip-icon { font-size: 1.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }

  .equip-name {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text-dark);
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .equip-note {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  /* ── Recipe Card ── */
  .recipe-card {
    background: var(--dark);
    border-radius: 18px;
    padding: 2rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .recipe-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .recipe-item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.25rem;
  }

  .recipe-val {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--amber);
  }

  .recipe-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: rgba(250,247,242,0.4);
  }

  /* ── Steps Timeline ── */
  .steps {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
  }

  .step {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .step-marker {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .step-num {
    width: 36px;
    height: 36px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--dark);
    color: var(--amber);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .step-line {
    width: 2px;
    flex: 1;
    background: var(--border-subtle);
    min-height: 20px;
  }

  .step:last-child .step-line { display: none; }

  .step-body {
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    flex: 1;
  }

  .step:last-child .step-body { padding-bottom: 0; }

  .step-time {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--amber);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .step-body h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--text-dark);
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem !important;
  }

  .step-body p {
    font-size: 0.95rem !important;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem !important;
  }

  .step-detail {
    background: rgba(196,123,48,0.06);
    border: 1px solid rgba(196,123,48,0.12);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .step-detail strong { color: var(--text-dark); }

  /* ── Bed Reading ── */
  .bed-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .bed-card {
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .bed-visual {
    height: 60px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    justify-content: center;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding: 0 1rem;
  }

  .bed-line {
    width: 100%;
    height: 3px;
    background: var(--brown);
    border-radius: 2px;
    position: relative;
  }

  .bed-line--flat { border-radius: 2px; }

  .bed-line--dome {
    height: 30px;
    background: transparent;
    border: 3px solid var(--brown);
    border-bottom: 3px solid var(--brown);
    border-radius: 50% 50% 0 0;
  }

  .bed-line--crater {
    height: 20px;
    background: transparent;
    border: 3px solid var(--brown);
    border-top: none;
    border-radius: 0 0 50% 50%;
  }

  .bed-card h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.375rem !important;
  }

  .bed-card p {
    font-size: 0.82rem !important;
    margin: 0 !important;
  }

  .bed-card--good { border-color: rgba(22,163,74,0.2); }

  /* ── Troubleshooting ── */
  .trouble-table {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .tt-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }

  .tt-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  .tt-problem {
    color: var(--text-dark);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .tt-cause { color: var(--text-muted); }

  .tt-fix {
    color: var(--brown);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  /* ── Tip Callout ── */
  .tip-callout {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
    background: rgba(196,123,48,0.06);
    border: 1px solid rgba(196,123,48,0.15);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .tip-icon { font-size: 1.25rem; flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 0.1rem; }
  .tip-callout strong { color: var(--text-dark); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .equipment-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
    .recipe-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
    .bed-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .tt-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.25rem; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .equipment-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }

  .tool-promo { margin: 2.5rem 0; }

  .tool-promo a {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    padding: 1.2rem 1.4rem;
    background: rgba(196,123,48,0.07);
    border: 1px solid rgba(196,123,48,0.22);
    border-radius: 14px;
    transition: border-color 0.2s, background 0.2s;
  }

  .tool-promo a:hover { border-color: var(--amber); background: rgba(196,123,48,0.11); }
  .tool-promo a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--amber); outline-offset: 2px; }

  .tool-promo .tp-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.11em;
    color: var(--amber);
  }

  .tool-promo .tp-desc { font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-muted); }
</style>
